# %% [markdown]
# # IMDB Sentiment Analysis - Week 1: Exploratory Data Analysis
#
# ## Objective
#
# The main goal of Week 1 is to understand the IMDB dataset, explore its structure,
# check sentiment distribution, analyze review lengths, and prepare the project for
# preprocessing and modeling.

# %%
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import seaborn as sns

# %% [markdown]
# ## Loading the Dataset

# %%
df = pd.read_csv("../data/IMDB Dataset.csv")
df.head()

# %% [markdown]
# ## Dataset Shape

# %%
df.shape

# %% [markdown]
# The dataset contains 50,000 rows and 2 columns: `review` and `sentiment`.

# %%
df.info()

# %% [markdown]
# ## Checking Missing Values

# %%
df.isnull().sum()

# %% [markdown]
# There are no missing values in the dataset, which makes the dataset clean and ready for further preprocessing.

# %% [markdown]
# ## Sentiment Distribution

# %%
df["sentiment"].value_counts()

# %%
plt.figure(figsize=(6, 4))
sns.countplot(x="sentiment", data=df)
plt.title("Sentiment Distribution")
plt.xlabel("Sentiment")
plt.ylabel("Count")
plt.show()

# %% [markdown]
# The dataset is perfectly balanced because it contains 25,000 positive and 25,000 negative reviews.

# %% [markdown]
# ## Example Positive Review

# %%
positive_review = df[df["sentiment"] == "positive"]["review"].iloc[0]
print(positive_review)

# %% [markdown]
# ## Example Negative Review

# %%
negative_review = df[df["sentiment"] == "negative"]["review"].iloc[0]
print(negative_review)

# %% [markdown]
# ## Review Length Analysis

# %%
df["review_length"] = df["review"].apply(len)
df["review_length"].describe()

# %%
plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))
sns.histplot(df["review_length"], bins=50)
plt.title("Distribution of Review Lengths")
plt.xlabel("Review Length")
plt.ylabel("Frequency")
plt.show()

# %% [markdown]
# The review lengths are different. Some reviews are short, while others are very long.
# This means that during preprocessing we may need padding and truncation.

# %% [markdown]
# ## Average Review Length by Sentiment

# %%
df.groupby("sentiment")["review_length"].mean()

# %%
plt.figure(figsize=(6, 4))
sns.barplot(x="sentiment", y="review_length", data=df)
plt.title("Average Review Length by Sentiment")
plt.xlabel("Sentiment")
plt.ylabel("Average Review Length")
plt.show()

# %% [markdown]
# ## Conclusion
#
# In Week 1, I explored the IMDB dataset and understood its basic structure.
# The dataset is clean, balanced, and suitable for sentiment analysis.
# The next step is text preprocessing and building a baseline model.
